  "sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://inventaris.onroerenderfgoed.be/erfgoedobjecten/24555",
      "inspection": "Primary heritage record read: rectangular Tournai-limestone Gothic tower; three stages of paired pointed windows, seven stringcourses; twenty gargoyles/four watchmen, polygonal corner towers, lower gallery and open clock arches/upper gallery. Current stone crown1911–1913. Its1976scaffolding statement is historical, not current appearance. Dragon nearly3m long."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://inventaris.onroerenderfgoed.be/erfgoedobjecten/24556",
      "inspection": "Primary record read: attached rectangular three-story Cloth Hall, eleven bays/eleven stepped dormers and eleven timber dormers each slope, four projecting octagonal corner turrets, slate gabled roof. South five-bay gable with split approach stair and Gothic portal. West side former jail annex retained. Current facade proportions estimated from photographs/native outline."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://historischehuizen.stad.gent/nl/belfort/bezoek/groep",
      "inspection": "Current City Historic Houses page actually read: nominal tower height95m. Matches native height95m; retained as nominal top control. Qualla text says91m and City dragon article quotes101–103m; these conflict, so height is not claimed as surveyed."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://visit.gent.be/en/see-do/ghent-belfry",
      "inspection": "Official tourism page actually read: attached Cloth Hall/Mammelokker identity and former jail entrance1741. Describes hall completed1907, while heritage record says four bays added1903; dates retained as source disagreement, not geometry difference."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://stad.gent/nl/magazine/nieuws-evenementen/gemaakt-gent-de-draak-op-het-belfort",
      "inspection": "City2024article actually read: current gilded copper dragon is third version, made1980, previous dragon displayed inside. Fine figure simplified; no museum fixture modeled. Anecdotal quoted101–103m heights conflict with same operator95m/control and Qualla91m; no unqualified survey claim."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.google.com/maps/@51.05366,3.72488,20z/data=!3m1!1e3",
      "inspection": "Current aerial actually inspected: tower against west long side of NE-aligned Cloth Hall, own small Mammelokker annex fartherNEon west edge. Native tower/hall/annex match. Fountain, independent market pavilion35184506955379/35184873561464 and neighborhood excluded. Story coordinate lies~40mNEof tower; placement uses actual tower native center."
    }
  ],
